# The one and only prettierignore in this repo.
#
# Prettier does NOT walk up the tree looking for this file the way it does for
# .prettierrc — it reads whichever one sits in the directory it was invoked from
# and ignores the rest. A second copy inside frontend/ is what previously meant
# these rules silently did not apply to any hook that ran from the root.
#
# Patterns here resolve relative to THIS file, so frontend/'s scripts point at it
# with `--ignore-path ../.prettierignore` and get results identical to a run
# started at the root.
#
# This file is deliberately short. Everything generated or untracked is already
# ignored via `--ignore-path ../.gitignore`, which the prettier scripts pass
# alongside this one. That only works because the repo now has exactly one
# .gitignore — prettier reads the single file it is handed rather than walking
# the tree, so a nested one would be silently skipped. Listed below is only what
# git tracks but prettier must not touch.

# The Angular app. Read-only reference material for the React migration, deleted
# at the end of it. Never formatted, linted, built or tested — see CLAUDE.md.
angular-frontend/

# Generated, and committed. Regenerating is the only correct way to change these;
# reformatting puts the working tree permanently at odds with the generator.
backend/openapi.json
frontend/src/**/generated/

# Lockfiles are npm's to format, not ours.
**/package-lock.json
